      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t know if the stock platform supports multiple sim devices. I can see two possibilities before my change:\n\n1) The time / time zone code is run for both, leading to flip-flopping if the two carriers disagree.\n2) The time / time zone code is run for only one of them.\n\nI don\u0027t think anything I\u0027m doing here will change the behavior but that\u0027s mostly a guess.\n\nhallliu@ - do we have any insight into dual sim devices or is it all managed by OEM-level customization?\n\nFTR - if it\u0027s something we need to deal with my thought was to have separate sources (NITZ_SIM1 / NITZ_SIM2), or add metadata to the TimeSignal to indicate the sim ID. Either way, once the information is there the time detector service can decide what to do once we know: prioritize one over the other, ignore sim 2, etc.",
